      "run": 2,
      "steps": 4,
      "narrative": "I found myself in a dimly lit, cramped galley, where the relentless intrusion of salt had permeated every crevice. Two paths stood before me: a north-bound doorway and a hatch leading downwards into the south. My investigation led me to discover a kettle lying lifeless on the salty floor. With a sense of purpose, I scooped up the kettle, considering its potential uses. My curiosity piqued, I attempted to open the hatch, but found it unyielding. In my haste, I had overlooked a crucial detail and was unable to open it. After a brief moment of contemplation, I opted to close the hatch, deciding against any further attempt for now. Throughout my brief sojourn, I've been navigating this environment as a curious explorer, cautiously examining my surroundings, and interacting with objects to uncover their purpose and utility.",
